ll","category":"viewpoint","tags":["views","hiking","photo"],"location":{"lat":55.78694,"lng":-2.05139},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"berwick_upon_tweed_halidon_hill","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":8,"wikiPageviews":139,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["halidonhill","berwickupontweed"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Halidon Hill is a summit, about 2 miles (3 km) west of the centre of Berwick-upon-Tweed, on the border of England and Scotland. It reaches 600 feet (180 m) high. The name of the hill indicates that it once had a fortification on its top. It is bounded by the A6105 road on its south and the A1 road to the northeast.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Halidon Hill","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Halidon_Hill_battle_site_-_geograph.org.uk_-_635309.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Halidon_Hill_battle_site_-_geograph.org.uk_-_635309.jpg","w":1200,"h":801,"author":"Lisa Jarvis","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Halidon_Hill_battle_site_-_geograph.org.uk_-_635309.jpg"}},{"id":"berwick_upon_tweed_edrington","areaId":"berwick_upon_tweed","name":"Edrington","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo","views"],"location":{"lat":55.77389,"lng":-2.09528},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"berwick_upon_tweed_edrington","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":6,"wikiPageviews":134,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["edrington","berwickupontweed"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Edrington is a medieval estate occupying the lower part of Mordington parish in Berwickshire, Scotland, five miles (8.0 km) west of Berwick-upon-Tweed. From probably the 14th century, if not earlier, a castle occupied the steep hill above the mill of the same name on the Whiteadder Water.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Edrington","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Edrington_castle_%26_mill.jpg/1280px-Edrington_castle_%26_mill.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Edrington_castle_%26_mill.jpg/500px-Edrington_castle_%26_mill.jpg","w":1200,"h":992,"author":"It is in family possession (agreed to copy it) and obviously well out of copyrig","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edrington_castle_%26_mill.jpg"}},{"id":"berwick_upon_tweed_berwick_lighthouse","areaId":"berwick_upon_tweed","name":"Berwick Lighthouse","category":"landmark","tags":["sea","views","photo"],"location":{"lat":55.76477,"lng":-1.98515},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"berwick_upon_tweed_berwick_lighthouse","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":100,"wikiPageviews":16,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["berwicklighthouse","berwickupontweed"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Berwick-upon-Tweed, sometimes known as Berwick-on-Tweed or simply Berwick, is a town and civil parish in Northumberland, England. It lies 2.5 mi (4 km) south of the Anglo-Scottish border and is the northernmost town in England. The 2011 census recorded Berwick's population as 12,043.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Berwick Lighthouse","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Berwick_Lighthouse_geograph_-_3317786.jpg/1280px-Berwick_Lighthouse_geograph_-_3317786.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Berwick_Lighthouse_geograph_-_3317786.jpg/500px-Berwick_Lighthouse_geograph_-_3317786.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Barbara Carr","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berwick_Lighthouse_geograph_-_3317786.jpg"}},{"id":"berwick_upon_tweed_shielfield_park","areaId":"berwick_upon_tweed","name":"Shielfield Park","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":55.76,"lng":-2.01583},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"berwick_upon_tweed_shielfield_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":5,"commonsNearby":6,"wikiPageviews":590,"wikidataSitelinks":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["shielfieldpark","berwickupontweed"],"summary":"Shielfield Park is a football stadium that is home to Berwick Rangers and Berwick Bandits speedway team. Although Berwick Rangers is a Scottish Lowland Football League club, Shielfield Park is situated in the English county of Northumberland.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Shielfield Park","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Shielfield_Park%2C_Home_of_Berwick_Rangers_FC_-_geograph.org.uk_-_409958.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Shielfield_Park%2C_Home_of_Berwick_Rangers_FC_-_geograph.org.uk_-_409958.jpg","w":1200,"h":844,"author":"David Neill","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shielfield_Park,_Home_of_Berwick_Rangers_FC_-_geograph.org.uk_-_409958.jpg"}},{"id":"berwick_upon_tweed_osm_viewpoint_map","areaId":"berwick_upon_tweed","name":"Viewpoint map","category":"viewpoint","tags":["views","photo","sunset"],"location":{"lat":55.8069,"lng":-2.04254},"visitMinutes":45,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"berwick_upon_tweed_osm_viewpoint_map","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":60,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["viewpointmap","berwickupontweed"],"bestLight":"sunset","photo":